  {
    "text": "Clear All",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/?ea735457_page=12"
  },
  {
    "text": "UX DesignerA UX designer is responsible for how a product feels to use: the flow, structure, and logic of the experience. Learn what they do and how the role differs from a product manager.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/ux-designer"
  },
  {
    "text": "Value PropositionWhat is a value proposition? Learn how to develop and write a strong value proposition and why it's essential for product managers.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/value-proposition"
  },
  {
    "text": "Value vs. ComplexityWhat is the Value vs. Complexity prioritization model and how can you use it? Learn the 3 steps for this prioritization matrix.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/value-vs-complexity"
  },
  {
    "text": "Vanity MetricsVanity metrics are statistics that look spectacular on the surface but don\u2019t necessarily translate to any meaningful business results.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/vanity-metrics"
  },
  {
    "text": "VelocityWhat is Velocity in product management? Discover the definition and when agile development teams use velocity in their sprint cycles.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/velocity"
  },
  {
    "text": "Voice of Customer (VoC)What is Voice of Customer (VoC)? Learn more about Voice of Customer (VoC) and other product management terms in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/voice-of-customer"
  },
  {
    "text": "WaterfallWhat is Waterfall in product development? Learn more about Waterfall, Agile and other product management terms in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/waterfall"
  },
  {
    "text": "Weighted ScoringWeighted scoring prioritization uses numerical scoring to rank your strategic initiatives against benefit and cost categories. It is helpful for product teams looking for objective prioritization techniques that factor in multiple layers of data.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/weighted-scoring"
  },
  {
    "text": "Weighted Shortest Job First (WSJF)Weighted Shortest Job First (WSJF) is an agile tool used to help teams prioritize a list of initiatives. We explain how your team can use WSJF.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/weighted-shortest-job-first"
  },
  {
    "text": "What is a BacklogA backlog is a list of tasks required to support a larger strategic plan. A well-maintained backlog has items ordered by priority.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/what-is-a-backlog"
  },
  {
    "text": "What Is a Product Engagement Score?What is a product engagement score (PES)? It measures how a user interacts with your product and helps define the customer experience.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/product-engagement-score"
  },
  {
    "text": "What Is a Product Operating Model?Product operating models help teams deliver the greatest value to customers, by centering it around the product's functions and operations.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/product-operating-model"
  },
  {
    "text": "WireframeWhat is a wireframe and why do they matter to product managers? Learn more about wireframes and other product management terms in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/wireframe"
  },
  {
    "text": "Working Backwards (the Amazon Method)The Amazon working backward method is a product development approach that starts with the team imagining the product is ready to ship.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/working-backward-amazon-method"
  },
